## 🗄️ Database Schema

| Table | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `robots` | Robot info (id, name, status, x, y, battery, zone) |
| `tasks` | Tasks (id, type, priority, source, destination, status) |
| `agent_logs` | Every agent decision (agent_name, action, reasoning) |
| `battery_logs` | Battery history + charging events |
| `collision_events` | Collision detection records |
| `zones` | Warehouse zones (id, name, coordinates, type) |
| `charging_stations` | Charging station locations |
| `users` | Authentication (username, password_hash, role) |
| `simulation_runs` | Simulation history |

---

## 🔌 API Endpoints

### Robots
- `GET /api/robots` — list all robots
- `GET /api/robots/{id}` — get robot details
- `POST /api/robots` — add new robot
- `PUT /api/robots/{id}` — update robot
- `DELETE /api/robots/{id}` — remove robot

### Tasks
- `GET /api/tasks` — list all tasks
- `POST /api/tasks` — create task
- `PUT /api/tasks/{id}/assign` — assign task to robot
- `PUT /api/tasks/{id}/complete` — mark complete

### Agents
- `GET /api/agents` — list all agents + status
- `GET /api/agents/{name}/logs` — agent decision logs
- `POST /api/agents/{name}/reason` — ask agent to reason via Gemini

### Battery
- `GET /api/battery/status` — all robots' battery
- `POST /api/battery/charge/{robot_id}` — send to charging

### Collision
- `GET /api/collision/events` — all collision events
- `GET /api/collision/heatmap` — heatmap data

### Simulation
- `POST /api/simulation/start`
- `POST /api/simulation/pause`
- `POST /api/simulation/reset`

### WebSocket
- `WS /ws/fleet` — live robot + agent updates

**Full interactive docs available at:** `http://localhost:8000/docs`

---

## ⚙️ Installation & Setup

### Prerequisites
- Python 3.10+
- Node.js 18+
- Git
- Google Gemini API Key ([Get free key](https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey))

### 🔧 Backend Setup

```bash
# 1. Clone repo
git clone https://github.com/vishakha2121/Multi-Agent-Robotics-Fleet-Coordination-Platform.git
cd Multi-Agent-Robotics-Fleet-Coordination-Platform/backend

# 2. Create virtual environment
python -m venv venv

# Windows
venv\Scripts\activate

# Mac/Linux
source venv/bin/activate

# 3. Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 4. Setup environment
copy .env.example .env
# Edit .env and add your GEMINI_API_KEY

# 5. Initialize database
python database/init_db.py

# 6. Seed sample data (100 robots + tasks)
python database/seed_data.py

# 7. Run server
uvicorn main:app --reload --port 8000
```

Backend running at: `http://localhost:8000`
API Docs: `http://localhost:8000/docs`

### 🎨 Frontend Setup

```bash
# 1. Go to frontend
cd ../frontend

# 2. Install dependencies
npm install

# 3. Setup environment
copy .env.example .env
# Set VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000

# 4. Run dev server
npm run dev
```

Frontend running at: `http://localhost:5173`

---

## 🔐 Environment Variables

### Backend `.env`
```env
# App
APP_NAME=Multi-Agent Robotics Fleet Platform
DEBUG=True
SECRET_KEY=your-secret-key-here

# Database
DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./database/fleet.db

# Gemini AI
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-1.5-flash

# Simulation
SIMULATION_TICK_MS=500
MAX_ROBOTS=100
GRID_WIDTH=50
GRID_HEIGHT=50

# CORS
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173
```

### Frontend `.env`
```env
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
VITE_WS_URL=ws://localhost:8000/ws/fleet
```

---

## 🔄 How It Works

```
1. User creates a task: "Move box from Zone A to Zone B"
        ↓
2. TASK ALLOCATION AGENT picks the best robot (R-07)
        ↓
3. NAVIGATION AGENT calculates path: A → corridor → B
        ↓
4. COLLISION AVOIDANCE AGENT checks path is clear
        ↓
5. BATTERY AGENT confirms R-07 has enough charge
        ↓
6. FLEET SUPERVISOR AGENT approves the plan
        ↓
7. Simulation engine moves R-07 step-by-step
        ↓
8. WebSocket pushes updates to React dashboard
        ↓
9. User watches robot move live on the map
        ↓
10. Task completed → logs recorded → next task assigned
```

